This package is the Godot extension for Pithagoras: its browser half (web/), its server half (lib/server.js), built
from godot/src and shared/ in https://github.com/prometheion/pithagoras-extensions, and the pages its server half serves
(pages/). shared/docker-api.ts there is a copy of types from Pithagoras (https://github.com/thecodacus/pithagoras,
Apache-2.0). web/client.js bundles icons from react-icons (https://github.com/react-icons/react-icons, MIT), drawn from
Lucide (https://lucide.dev, ISC).

pages/stream holds Selkies 2.1.0's web client, by the Selkies Project, unchanged, under the Mozilla Public License 2.0
(pages/stream/LICENSE); its source is https://github.com/selkies-project/selkies/tree/2.1.0. The server half serves its
index.html with one script tag added to the head, which loads pages/stream/__gs_shim.js, this package's own file.

The package contains no Godot. The container image it runs, ghcr.io/prometheion/pithagoras-godot, is built from
godot/server in the same repository and redistributes Godot (MIT), Selkies, pixelflux and pcmflux (MPL-2.0, pixelflux
bundling x264 and x265 under the GPL and libde265 under the LGPL, pcmflux bundling libraries under the LGPL), VirtualGL
(wxWindows Library Licence) and Ubuntu packages, each under its own licence:
see godot/server/NOTICE in the repository and /usr/share/doc/pithagoras-godot in the image.

Not made or endorsed by the Godot Foundation. "Godot" names what the extension runs.
